{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ProposedViewSize","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"During layout in OpenSwiftUI, views choose their own size, but they do that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in response to a size proposal from their parent view. When you create","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a custom layout using the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" protocol, your layout container","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"participates in this process using ","type":"text"},{"code":"ProposedViewSize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instances.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The layout protocol’s methods take a proposed size input that you","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can take into account when arranging views and calculating the size of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the composite container. Similarly, your layout proposes a size to each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of its own subviews when it measures and places them.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Layout containers typically measure their subviews by proposing several","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sizes and looking at the responses. The container can use this information","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to decide how to allocate space among its subviews. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"layout might try the following special proposals:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ProposedViewSize\/zero"},{"type":"text","text":" proposal; the view responds with its minimum size."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ProposedViewSize\/infinity"},{"type":"text","text":" proposal; the view responds with its maximum size."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ProposedViewSize\/unspecified"},{"type":"text","text":" proposal; the view responds with its ideal size."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A layout might also try special cases for one dimension at a time. For","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"example, an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HStack","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" might measure the flexibility of its subviews’","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"widths, while using a fixed value for the height.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI"]]},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Operators","anchor":"Operators","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ProposedViewSize\/==(_:_:)"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ProposedViewSize\/init(_:)","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ProposedViewSize\/init(width:height:)"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ProposedViewSize\/height","doc: